---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Field from '../components/Field.astro';
---
<Base title="Playground" description="Run Hale examples in the browser, precompiled to WebAssembly.">
  <Field />
  <section class="wrap page">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>Run Hale in the browser</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Curated Hale programs, precompiled to WebAssembly by the compiler
        you would install, run entirely in the browser. The gallery runs
        them as written; editing your own source here waits on the compile
        service, which is offline for now.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="play-frame">
      <iframe src="/play/" title="Hale example gallery" loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/play/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open full screen ↗</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/docs/getting-started/install">Install locally</a>
    </div>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:var(--s12)">
      <ul class="facts">
        <li><b>The tour</b><p>Starts with ordinary functions and ends with loci, typed topics, supervision and deployment, without changing tools.</p></li>
        <li><b>What runs</b><p>The portable standard library and the typed bus, as they do natively. The syscall-backed namespaces are refused at compile time inside the sandbox, with the reason.</p></li>
        <li><b>Locally</b><p>The install line on the <a href="/">front page</a> puts the same compiler on Linux or macOS.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
